<Base title="About" description="Who makes the Spectrum Atlas, under which licences, and how to cite it.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>Spectrum Atlas is the public front door of one research pipeline: infrared spectra of molecules, corrected by a learned layer that is trained on coupled-cluster anchors, with the status and the provenance of every number. It is built as a capstone project and documented in the open.</p>
  <h2>Licences</h2>
  <p>Data: CC BY 4.0. Code: MIT. Reading, browsing and downloading need no account; sign-in will be asked only of people who want to feed the pipeline (request a run, submit a molecule).</p>
  <h2>Cite</h2>
  <p class="muted">A Zenodo DOI follows the first data release; until then cite the repository.</p>
  <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/thebreadishard/udacity-capstone-plan">The repository</a> — plans, probes, modules, ledgers.</li>
    <li><a href="https://thebreadishard.github.io/">The lab notebook</a> — the story in plain English.</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.astrochem.org/pahdb/">NASA Ames PAHdb</a> — the reference library this atlas complements and links to.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>No trackers, no cookies, no analytics. The site is static.</p>
</Base>
